# Rigor core overlay — supplemental core signatures.
#
# --- Hash.ruby2_keywords_hash? / Hash.ruby2_keywords_hash ---
#
# CRuby's `hash.c` defines both as singleton methods of `Hash`, present since
# Ruby 2.7:
#
#   rb_define_singleton_method(rb_cHash, "ruby2_keywords_hash?", rb_hash_s_ruby2_keywords_hash_p, 1);
#   rb_define_singleton_method(rb_cHash, "ruby2_keywords_hash", rb_hash_s_ruby2_keywords_hash, 1);
#
# `ruby2_keywords_hash?` answers whether the argument is a hash flagged by
# `ruby2_keywords`; `ruby2_keywords_hash` returns a copy of its argument with
# that flag set. Upstream `ruby/rbs` declares neither through 4.2, so
#
#   Hash.ruby2_keywords_hash?({})
#
# reported `call.undefined-method` on correct code. Ruby 4.1 deprecates both
# (Feature #22205) and removes them in 4.5; `call.deprecated-ruby2-keywords`
# reports the deprecation under an explicit `target_ruby` of 4.1 or later.
#
# The return of `ruby2_keywords_hash` is the argument's own Hash type: the
# copy has the same keys and values, and the flag does not show in the type.
#
# Declared on a module `Hash` extends, not with `def self.…`, for the reason
# `process.rbs` gives: a project `sig/` or a later rbs release may declare
# either method directly, and a second direct `def` is a
# `DuplicatedMethodDefinitionError` that takes `Hash`'s whole singleton surface
# down to `Dynamic[top]`. A direct `def` overrides a method `Hash` gets through
# `extend`, so the overlay stands down instead of colliding.
#
# Unconditional, not gated on `target_ruby` or the rbs line: both methods exist
# on every supported Ruby (2.7 through 4.4), and gating would report
# `call.undefined-method` on a correct project still on the default
# `target_ruby`. The deprecation for 4.1+ is a separate rule and does not read
# this declaration.
module RigorCoreOverlay
  module HashRuby2Keywords
    def ruby2_keywords_hash?: (Hash[untyped, untyped]) -> bool
    def ruby2_keywords_hash: [K, V] (Hash[K, V]) -> Hash[K, V]
  end
end

class Hash[unchecked out K, unchecked out V]
  extend RigorCoreOverlay::HashRuby2Keywords
end
